  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 2.888,
      "text": "Reading a table is only half the job.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 2.888,
      "end": 8.125,
      "text": "You also create it, fill it, change it, and sometimes throw a column away.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 8.125,
      "end": 10.555,
      "text": "Until now the table felt like a given.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 10.555,
      "end": 13.305,
      "text": "Someone else had already named the columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 13.305,
      "end": 14.722,
      "text": "Now you are the someone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 14.722,
      "end": 18.805,
      "text": "CREATE TABLE names the table and lists columns with types.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 18.805,
      "end": 22.138,
      "text": "Each column is one attribute you promise to store.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 22.138,
      "end": 25.0,
      "text": "customer_id is an integer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 26.347,
      "text": "name is text.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 26.347,
      "end": 27.819,
      "text": "city is text.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 27.819,
      "end": 29.625,
      "text": "That list is a contract.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 29.625,
      "end": 32.0,
      "text": "Rows that arrive later have to fit it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 32.0,
      "end": 33.597,
      "text": "INSERT adds a row.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 33.597,
      "end": 37.68,
      "text": "You list the columns, then the values, in the same order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 37.68,
      "end": 42.291,
      "text": "A second INSERT is a second customer \u2014 not an edit of the first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 42.291,
      "end": 43.722,
      "text": "Maya is one row.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 43.722,
      "end": 45.111,
      "text": "Jordan is another.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 45.111,
      "end": 50.027,
      "text": "If you insert Maya twice, you now have two Mayas unless a key stops you.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 50.027,
      "end": 53.138,
      "text": "UPDATE changes values already in the table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 53.138,
      "end": 55.111,
      "text": "SET names the new value.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 55.111,
      "end": 57.083,
      "text": "WHERE names which rows move.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 57.083,
      "end": 60.972,
      "text": "Always pair UPDATE with WHERE, or every row moves.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 60.972,
      "end": 62.916,
      "text": "That is the classic accident.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 62.916,
      "end": 64.625,
      "text": "You meant Sofia's city.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 64.625,
      "end": 66.541,
      "text": "You rewrote the whole column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 66.541,
      "end": 68.486,
      "text": "DELETE removes rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 68.486,
      "end": 71.972,
      "text": "Again: WHERE, or the table goes quiet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 71.972,
      "end": 75.861,
      "text": "DELETE FROM customers with no filter is not bravery.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 75.861,
      "end": 77.027,
      "text": "It is a wipe.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 77.027,
      "end": 79.236,
      "text": "SELECT first when you are unsure.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 79.236,
      "end": 81.375,
      "text": "See the rows the WHERE would catch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 81.375,
      "end": 82.513,
      "text": "Then change them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 82.513,
      "end": 86.125,
      "text": "ALTER TABLE adds a column when the world changes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 86.125,
      "end": 88.069,
      "text": "Maybe you now store an email.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 88.069,
      "end": 91.833,
      "text": "Existing rows get NULL unless you supply a default.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 91.833,
      "end": 94.083,
      "text": "ALTER can also rename a column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 94.083,
      "end": 95.527,
      "text": "It can drop a column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 95.527,
      "end": 98.402,
      "text": "Dropping a column throws the values away.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 98.402,
      "end": 101.375,
      "text": "There is no undo in the statement itself.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 101.375,
      "end": 104.222,
      "text": "DROP TABLE removes the table itself.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 104.222,
      "end": 105.902,
      "text": "That is not a row delete.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 105.902,
      "end": 107.625,
      "text": "The whole object is gone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 107.625,
      "end": 110.638,
      "text": "The name, the columns, the rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 110.638,
      "end": 112.833,
      "text": "Think of CREATE as the shape.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 112.833,
      "end": 114.958,
      "text": "INSERT as the first facts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.958,
      "end": 116.666,
      "text": "UPDATE as a correction.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 116.666,
      "end": 119.166,
      "text": "DELETE as a removal of a fact.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 119.166,
      "end": 121.666,
      "text": "ALTER as a later change to the shape.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 121.666,
      "end": 124.263,
      "text": "DROP as taking the object off the shelf.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 124.263,
      "end": 127.666,
      "text": "Practice on a copy, not the only copy you have.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 127.666,
      "end": 129.388,
      "text": "Insert two rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 129.388,
      "end": 130.486,
      "text": "Update one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 130.486,
      "end": 131.722,
      "text": "Delete the other.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 131.722,
      "end": 133.361,
      "text": "Select to see the shape.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 133.361,
      "end": 135.736,
      "text": "If ALTER feels scary, it should.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 135.736,
      "end": 139.0,
      "text": "You are changing the contract other queries depend on.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 139.0,
      "end": 141.43,
      "text": "Write the dangerous statements slowly.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 141.43,
      "end": 143.152,
      "text": "Read the WHERE twice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 143.152,
      "end": 145.722,
      "text": "Then the table stays a place you can trust.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 145.722,
      "end": 151.402,
      "text": "Transactions belong with this family of verbs, even if they get their own later lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 151.402,
      "end": 156.847,
      "text": "BEGIN, then INSERT, then a SELECT that looks wrong, then ROLLBACK.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 156.847,
      "end": 158.833,
      "text": "The table forgets the insert.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 158.833,
      "end": 160.43,
      "text": "COMMIT is how you keep it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 160.43,
      "end": 164.597,
      "text": "Until you commit, another session may not see your rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 164.597,
      "end": 166.972,
      "text": "That is a feature when you are still deciding.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 166.972,
      "end": 171.111,
      "text": "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is for scripts you run twice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 171.111,
      "end": 172.791,
      "text": "It is not a design tool.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 172.791,
      "end": 176.555,
      "text": "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS is for throwaway sandboxes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 176.555,
      "end": 179.652,
      "text": "It is not how a store retires a customer list.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 179.652,
      "end": 182.75,
      "text": "INSERT can take a SELECT instead of VALUES.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 182.75,
      "end": 185.375,
      "text": "That copies rows from a staging table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 185.375,
      "end": 187.597,
      "text": "Check the column order twice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 187.597,
      "end": 191.944,
      "text": "UPDATE can use a join in some dialects to patch from another table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 191.944,
      "end": 195.611,
      "text": "In SQLite you often write a subquery in SET.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 195.611,
      "end": 196.944,
      "text": "Still use WHERE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 196.944,
      "end": 201.444,
      "text": "DELETE with a subquery can remove orphans you found on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 201.444,
      "end": 203.5,
      "text": "SELECT those orphans first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 203.5,
      "end": 206.638,
      "text": "Keep a backup file before a destructive script.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 206.638,
      "end": 209.152,
      "text": "A dump is cheaper than archaeology.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 209.152,
      "end": 211.902,
      "text": "Column types on ALTER vary by engine.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 211.902,
      "end": 217.111,
      "text": "SQLite will add a column and will not freely drop one in older versions.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 217.111,
      "end": 220.458,
      "text": "PostgreSQL will do more in one ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 220.458,
      "end": 223.625,
      "text": "Read the dialect before you promise a migration.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 223.625,
      "end": 227.68,
      "text": "Default values on a new column backfill old rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 227.68,
      "end": 232.68,
      "text": "Choose the default as if it were a historical fact, because it becomes one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 232.68,
      "end": 233.944,
      "text": "Rename with care.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 233.944,
      "end": 237.375,
      "text": "Queries you have not found yet still use the old name.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 237.375,
      "end": 238.722,
      "text": "The verbs are few.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 238.722,
      "end": 241.291,
      "text": "The damage is large when WHERE is missing.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 241.291,
      "end": 244.083,
      "text": "That is why this lesson is slow on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 244.083,
      "end": 247.555,
      "text": "Shape, facts, correction, removal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 247.555,
      "end": 250.208,
      "text": "Say which one you are doing before you type it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 250.208,
      "end": 254.097,
      "text": "Table work and row work are two families of verbs.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 254.097,
      "end": 257.555,
      "text": "CREATE and ALTER and DROP change the object.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 257.555,
      "end": 261.708,
      "text": "INSERT and UPDATE and DELETE change the facts inside it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 261.708,
      "end": 266.93,
      "text": "Mixing the families in your head is how DROP gets typed when DELETE was meant.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 266.93,
      "end": 272.013,
      "text": "CREATE TABLE starts with the name, then a list of columns in parentheses.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 272.013,
      "end": 274.694,
      "text": "Each column is a name, then a type.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 274.694,
      "end": 277.847,
      "text": "Lines in that list are separated by commas.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 277.847,
      "end": 282.138,
      "text": "The primary key is part of the contract, not a later wish.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 282.266,
      "end": 287.854,
      "text": "You can mark a column PRIMARY KEY on its line, or name the key in a separate line.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 287.854,
      "end": 292.896,
      "text": "Both mean: this value identifies the row, and it will not repeat.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 292.896,
      "end": 296.729,
      "text": "Types on CREATE are promises about what a cell may hold.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 296.729,
      "end": 300.229,
      "text": "A later INSERT that breaks the type is refused.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 300.229,
      "end": 302.785,
      "text": "That refusal is the point of the type.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 302.785,
      "end": 306.938,
      "text": "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is for a script you run twice.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 306.938,
      "end": 310.952,
      "text": "It will not fix a table you already created with the wrong columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 310.952,
      "end": 316.118,
      "text": "DROP TABLE removes the object: name, columns, rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 316.118,
      "end": 320.563,
      "text": "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS is for a sandbox you are allowed to destroy.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 320.563,
      "end": 323.257,
      "text": "It is not how a store retires customers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 323.257,
      "end": 327.771,
      "text": "INSERT lists columns, then VALUES, in the same order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 327.771,
      "end": 330.243,
      "text": "A second INSERT is a second row.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 330.243,
      "end": 335.896,
      "text": "If you omit the column list, you are betting the table's column order never changes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 335.896,
      "end": 337.313,
      "text": "Name the columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 337.313,
      "end": 342.327,
      "text": "INSERT can take a SELECT instead of VALUES when you copy from a staging table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 342.327,
      "end": 344.966,
      "text": "Check that copy with a SELECT first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 344.966,
      "end": 349.646,
      "text": "UPDATE names SET for the new value and WHERE for the rows that move.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 349.646,
      "end": 353.257,
      "text": "Without WHERE, every row takes the new value.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 353.257,
      "end": 356.591,
      "text": "That is the classic accident, and it is not rare.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 356.591,
      "end": 360.729,
      "text": "SELECT the same WHERE before you UPDATE, and look at the rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 360.729,
      "end": 361.868,
      "text": "Then change them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 361.868,
      "end": 364.716,
      "text": "DELETE removes rows that match WHERE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 364.716,
      "end": 368.66,
      "text": "Without WHERE, the table is empty and still exists.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 368.66,
      "end": 372.577,
      "text": "That is different from DROP, which removes the table itself.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 372.577,
      "end": 379.007,
      "text": "TRUNCATE, in engines that have it, empties rows as a bulk wipe and may reset counters.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 379.007,
      "end": 381.66,
      "text": "Know which verb you are holding before you run it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 381.66,
      "end": 389.813,
      "text": "ALTER TABLE changes the contract after the table already has friends: queries, views, application code.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 389.813,
      "end": 392.327,
      "text": "ADD COLUMN is the usual growth.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 392.327,
      "end": 397.924,
      "text": "Existing rows get NULL unless you supply a default, and that default becomes history.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 397.924,
      "end": 400.591,
      "text": "DROP COLUMN throws the values away.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 400.591,
      "end": 403.16,
      "text": "There is no undo in the statement.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 403.16,
      "end": 409.702,
      "text": "RENAME COLUMN breaks every query still using the old name, including ones you have not found yet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 409.702,
      "end": 414.188,
      "text": "Dialects disagree on how much ALTER can do in one trip.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 414.188,
      "end": 419.354,
      "text": "SQLite will add a column readily and historically fought dropping one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 419.354,
      "end": 422.896,
      "text": "PostgreSQL will do more in a single ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 422.896,
      "end": 426.341,
      "text": "Read the engine you are on before you promise a migration.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 426.341,
      "end": 433.716,
      "text": "BEGIN, then a change, then SELECT, then ROLLBACK, is how you practice without keeping the damage.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 433.716,
      "end": 435.313,
      "text": "COMMIT is how you keep it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 435.313,
      "end": 439.479,
      "text": "Until you commit, another session may not see your rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 439.479,
      "end": 442.799,
      "text": "That isolation is a feature while you are still deciding.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 442.799,
      "end": 449.077,
      "text": "Shape, facts, correction, removal, later shape, destruction of the object.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 449.077,
      "end": 451.16,
      "text": "Say which one you are doing out loud.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 451.16,
      "end": 453.285,
      "text": "Then type the verb that matches.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 453.285,
      "end": 458.216,
      "text": "The table stays a place you can trust when WHERE is present and DROP is rare.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 458.216,
      "end": 462.729,
      "text": "Table management commands: CREATE, ALTER, DROP.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 462.729,
      "end": 469.132,
      "text": "Data management commands: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and SELECT to verify.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 469.132,
      "end": 473.674,
      "text": "The lecture splits those families so you do not DROP when you meant DELETE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 473.674,
      "end": 477.757,
      "text": "CREATE needs a name and a column list and usually a key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 477.757,
      "end": 485.438,
      "text": "ALTER ADD is growth, ALTER DROP is loss, ALTER RENAME is a breaking change for callers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 485.438,
      "end": 490.979,
      "text": "INSERT adds facts, UPDATE edits facts, DELETE removes facts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 490.979,
      "end": 493.396,
      "text": "SELECT is how you look before you leap.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 493.396,
      "end": 500.368,
      "text": "Together they are the exact SQL you need to get a table installed and keep it honest, without a theory detour.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 500.368,
      "end": 507.257,
      "text": "Practice the families on a copy named customers_lab until the verbs feel different in your hands.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 507.257,
      "end": 510.091,
      "text": "Then use them on real names, slowly.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
